/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD rips Ole Miss, SEC; Rebels defend travel effort","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny ripped the SEC and Ole Miss for the \"inexplicable\" decision to move its game to Sunday, while the Rebels defended their travel efforts.","published":"2026-11-14T23:54:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Reynolds to have MRI on knee; backup Vizzina (ankle) also hurt","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds is having an MRI on his injured knee, and backup Christopher Vizzina was sent to the hospital to evaluate his ankle.","published":"2026-11-14T23:52:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State WR Smith sets Big Ten record, states Heisman case","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards while also making his Heisman Trophy case in Saturday's win over Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T23:15:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5088438/miquise-humphrey-grace","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mi%27Quise_Humphrey-Grace"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Mi'Quise Humphrey-Grace","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mi%27Quise_Humphrey-Grace","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:21Z","intro":"Mi'Quise Humphrey-Grace is an American college football defensive end for the Kentucky Wildcats. He previously played for the South Dakota Coyotes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Humphrey-Grace attended Princeton High School in Sharonville, Ohio. As a senior, he had 9.5 sacks. He committed to the University of South Dakota to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Humphrey-Grace played at South Dakota from 2022 to 2024. After redshirting his first year after playing in three games, he played in 13 games in 2023 and had 34 tackles, 5.5 sacks and one fumble recovery returned for a touchdown. In 2024, he was the Missouri Valley Football Conference (MVFC) Defensive Player of the Year after recording 59 tackles and a conference-leading 9.5 sacks over 14 starts. After the season, Humphrey-Grace entered the transfer portal and committed to the University of Kentucky. In his first year at Kentucky in 2025, he started all 12 games and had 31 tackles and a team leading 3.5 sacks. He returned to Kentucky as a starter in 2026."}]}}